  "<strong>Who wins, by board size.</strong> Tromp's table has 37 cells. The native solver attempted 29 and agrees on <strong>24</strong>; 5×10 (600 s), 9×5 (600 s), 10×5 (600 s), 10×4 (1500 s), 11×4 (600 s) hit the time cap. The other wide boards took Tromp thousands of CPU hours (9×6 in 2005, 8×8 in 2015) and were not attempted; 8×8 does not fit the 64-bit board.",
